Unfortunately, 7 requests for the same pallet type cannot be handled because there's only one AF standalone destacker, plus a F destacker (F is compatible to AF if AF is not available) and plus a U standalone destacker (U is compatible to AF if AF is not available), therefore system performance is limited by the limited number of empty AFs delivery points.

 Having more empty AF delivery points will produce two main positive effects:

- Picking performance increasing, aka reduction of pickers waiting time;
- Increasing the use of the cheapest pallet type (AF).

 According to this, the main idea principle is to create some special locations on the ground, capable to host stacks of empty AFs, and being reachable by both kinds of AGVs (ARTs and ATXs) and to let them to 'destack' a single AF from the stack on the ground, without any help of a mechanical device.

 ## 2.4.  Optimum number of empty pallets inside HBW1

We had noticed that  we  were  accumulating  many  empty  pallets  created  by  picking  stations.   We wanted to implement new parameters in FW028 in order to manage the number of empty pallets inside HBW1.

 Four new parameters were created for each type of empty pallets (created by negative pickings), named:

1. com.wamas.mfs.core.common.OptimumEmptyPalletTypeX: used to set optimum number of empty pallets X in HBW1;
2. com.wamas.mfs.core.common.OptimumEmptyPalletTypeU: used to set optimum number of empty pallets U in HBW1;
3. com.wamas.mfs.core.common.OptimumEmptyPalletTypeH: used to set optimum number of empty pallets H in HBW1;
4. com.wamas.mfs.core.common.OptimumEmptyPalletTypeD: used to set optimum number of empty pallets D in HBW1.

Unfortunately, 7 requests for the same pallet type cannot be handled because there's only one AF standalone destacker, plus a F destacker (F is compatible to AF if AF is not available) and plus a U standalone destacker (U is compatible to AF if AF is not available), therefore system performance is limited by the limited number of empty AFs delivery points.

 Having more empty AF delivery points will produce two main positive effects:

- Picking performance increasing, aka reduction of pickers waiting time;
- Increasing the use of the cheapest pallet type (AF).

 According to this, the main idea principle is to create some special locations on the ground, capable to host stacks of empty AFs, and being reachable by both kinds of AGVs (ARTs and ATXs) and to let them to 'destack' a single AF from the stack on the ground, without any help of a mechanical device.

